translate en b36_m19_a1:
    ageng "{i}(looking at the photo on Kai's phone){/i} This alley… dry. Been a long, long time since I saw it dry."

translate en b36_m19_a2:
    kai "Yeah, Pak. Feels weird. Like it's not even the same alley."

translate en b36_m19_a3:
    ageng "Same alley, kid. It's the person walking through it that changed."

translate en b36_m19_b1:
    ageng "{i}(listening to the footsteps recording from Kai's phone){/i} Your footsteps. No puddles. {i}(smiling faintly){/i} That's the sound of someone who isn't hiding from the rain anymore."

translate en b36_m19_b2:
    kai "…I wasn't hiding, Pak. Just— yeah. Maybe I was."

translate en b36r_001c:
    "No one says anything about it that afternoon. Kai walks straight in, sits down, and stays quiet — just like he has been lately."

translate en b36r_002:
    "Pak Ageng doesn't ask why Kai came. He just brews some tea and sits down. Lately Kai's been quiet more often than he talks, and Pak Ageng lets him be."

translate en b36r_003:
    "That night, an impatient knock hits Kai's front door. The second he opens it — Yara. No recorder. No headphones around her neck. Just a thin denim jacket, swollen eyes, a red nose."

translate en b36r_004:
    yara "Enough, Kai."

translate en b36r_005:
    "She steps inside without waiting to be invited. Kai takes a step back."

translate en b36r_006:
    yara "I need an answer. Right now. {i}(her voice trembling){/i} What did I do wrong? Tell me. What did I do so wrong that you suddenly threw me away like… like none of that time together meant anything?"

translate en b36r_007:
    kai_hati "She's crying. She's actually crying, right in front of me, right now. Not on a tape. Not on August first. Right now — because of me."

translate en b36r_008:
    kai "You didn't do anything wrong, Yara."

translate en b36r_009:
    yara "Then why?! {i}(half-shouting, tears spilling over){/i} Why do you look at me like you don't even know me? Why won't you listen to sounds with me anymore? You've been making me feel like I'm losing my mind, Kai. Walking around alone. For weeks."

translate en b36r_010:
    "Kai's fists clench tight. Inside his head, every cold excuse — \"it's to protect her\" — crumbles one by one."

translate en b36r_011a1:
    kai "Because I'm scared, Yara. {i}(taking a deep breath){/i} Sit down first. I'll tell you everything. Every crazy thing I've been hiding from you. Don't cut in yet, okay? Because if I stop halfway, I don't think I'll be able to finish."

translate en b36r_012a1:
    "In the quiet living room, Kai lays it all bare. His voice shakes, yet he doesn't stop."

translate en b36r_013a1:
    kai "Remember that cassette shop down the dead-end alley? Gema Masa. The tapes there… they play sounds from the future. Sixty seconds. At first it was just tomorrow. I got hooked, Yar. I was terrified out of my mind of tomorrow, so I just kept listening."

translate en b36r_014a1:
    kai "Back before we knew each other, I heard a tape that was completely silent. One full minute, nothing at all. I thought it meant I was gonna die that Friday. {i}(a short, bitter laugh){/i} Turns out it didn't. That silence was… the moment I saw you in the library. I didn't die, Yara. I actually felt alive, because of you."

translate en b36r_015a1:
    yara "{i}(silent, eyes wide, listening){/i}"

translate en b36r_016a1:
    kai "Then I found out you were leaving for university in six months. And I turned into a coward all over again. I bought the August first tape. I wanted to know… if you were still in my future or not."

translate en b36r_017a1:
    kai "{i}(looking down; tears falling onto his lap){/i} The price was my single happiest memory. And I paid it, Yara. I traded away the memory of the first time we met in the library. That's why I looked at you like a stranger. My brain knows you're Yara. My chest is just empty. The feeling's… gone."

translate en b36r_018a1:
    kai "All that was on the August first tape was you crying. Saying goodbye. So my stupid brain thought: if I push you away now, if we aren't that close anymore, the goodbye won't hurt as bad. For you. For me. I thought I was protecting you. Turns out I just… killed my own feelings."

translate en b36r_011a2:
    kai "Because I'm scared, Yara. {i}(a long pause){/i} I… listen. Sit down. Just sit down first. I'll tell you, just— bear with me, okay? I don't even know where to start."

translate en b36r_012a2:
    yara "Start anywhere, Kai. Just start."

translate en b36r_013a2:
    kai "That shop. Gema Masa. The tapes there… {i}(stopping; rubbing his face){/i} You're not gonna believe me."

translate en b36r_014a2:
    yara "Try me."

translate en b36r_015a2:
    kai "The tapes there can play sounds from the future. Sixty seconds. I… I bought them all the time. For the next day. Then there was a tape for August first, and I— {i}(his voice cracking){/i} I paid for it with my memory of the first time we met. At the library. The memory's gone, Yar. Actually gone. That's why I—"

translate en b36r_016a2:
    yara "{i}(softly){/i} …That's why you looked at me like a stranger."

translate en b36r_017a2:
    kai "Yeah. Yeah. And what was on the tape was you crying, saying goodbye. So I figured, if I backed off now, it wouldn't hurt as much later— {i}(stopping; shaking his head){/i} Stupid. I know it was stupid. I know."

translate en b36r_018a2:
    "Stumbling, broken into pieces, having to start over halfway through again and again — yet that night, for the first time, Kai doesn't stop until every word is out."

translate en b36r_011b:
    kai "{i}(staring down at the floor for a long time){/i} …I'm sorry, Yara."

translate en b36r_012b:
    yara "{i}(waiting){/i}"

translate en b36r_013b:
    kai "That's it. That's all."

translate en b36r_014b:
    yara "Sorry for what, Kai?"

translate en b36r_015b:
    "Kai opens his mouth. Closes it again. The words are right there — the shop, the tape, August first — yet all of them catch in his throat, just like always."

translate en b36r_016b:
    kai "Just… I'm sorry."

translate en b36r_017b:
    yara "{i}(nodding once, slowly){/i} Okay."

translate en b36r_018b:
    "She doesn't push. Doesn't ask again. She turns around, lets herself out, and walks away — leaving Kai with an apology that never explained a thing."

translate en b36r_011c:
    kai "{i}(shakes his head slowly; steps back; says nothing){/i}"

translate en b36r_012c:
    yara "{i}(looking at him for a long time){/i} …Okay. Okay, Kai."

translate en b36r_013c:
    "Yara nods like someone who just got her answer — because silence is an answer too. She leaves. The door clicks shut softly, hurting way worse than if she'd slammed it."

translate en b36s_001:
    "Yara arrives at the shop that afternoon brisk and bright-eyed — her official acceptance letter from the university in Yogyakarta just showed up. The moment she sees Kai, though, her steps slow."

translate en b36s_002:
    yara "Kai. Why're you… I've been talking this whole time and all you've given me is \"hm,\" \"oh,\" \"yeah.\" {i}(sitting down beside him){/i} Hey. What's wrong?"

translate en b36s_003:
    kai_hati "Tell her. Right now. Before it turns into something worse. While we can still talk it out with little laughs instead of tears."

translate en b36s_004:
    kai "Yar. There's something I wanna tell you. It's kinda… embarrassing, honestly."

translate en b36s_005:
    yara "{i}(tilting her head){/i} Who do you owe money to?"

translate en b36s_006:
    kai "Nobody. {i}(letting out a short, nervous laugh){/i} Listen first. {i}(pause){/i} I'm happy you got in. Seriously, really happy. You worked on that portfolio for months, I saw it myself. It's just… there's a part of me that's— {i}(stopping){/i}"

translate en b36s_007:
    yara "Scared."

translate en b36s_008:
    kai "{i}(going quiet){/i} …Yeah. Scared. August first sounds far away, except it isn't, Yar. It's fast. And I don't know what's gonna happen to us. I don't know what's gonna happen to me."

translate en b36s_009:
    yara "{i}(softly){/i} You think I'm not scared?"

translate en b36s_010:
    kai "You always look… brave."

translate en b36s_011:
    yara "Look is the word. {i}(smiling faintly){/i} Kai, I don't know what's gonna happen to us either. Nobody does. Want me to make some big dramatic promise? Can't do that. The only thing I can promise is this: I'm not disappearing without telling you. When I leave, you'll know what day, what train, what time. You can come see me off. You can cry too, I won't stop you."

translate en b36s_012:
    kai "{i}(laughing, genuinely this time){/i} …Sounds like a pretty rough deal for me."

translate en b36s_013:
    yara "It's an honest deal. {i}(standing up, patting Kai's shoulder once){/i} Alright. No more bottling it up, okay? If weird thoughts start spiraling, just tell me. I'm way better at answering real questions than guessing what's going on inside your head."

translate en b36s_014:
    ageng "{i}(from behind the counter, not looking up from the cassette he's cleaning){/i} Kids these days… your problem isn't that you don't have answers. Most of you are just too scared to ask."

translate en b36s_015:
    kai "Pak Ageng, were you listening this whole time?!"

translate en b36s_016:
    ageng "My shop's tiny, kid. {i}(smiling){/i} Wes, go on. Walk her home. Before it pours — once this alley clouds over, it doesn't waste any time."

translate en b36s_017:
    "At the mouth of the alley, Yara pauses for a moment. She looks up at the crooked wooden sign reading \"Gema Masa.\""

translate en b36s_018:
    yara "Kai. One more thing, while I'm thinking of it. {i}(pause){/i} Back then you mentioned there's a tape that lets you hear a year ahead. The one that costs… a memory."

translate en b36s_019:
    kai "{i}(falling silent){/i} …Yeah."

translate en b36s_020:
    yara "Did you ever think about buying it?"

translate en b36s_021:
    kai "{i}(taking a long moment to answer){/i} I did. Really seriously, actually. Practically had my hand on my wallet. {i}(a short laugh){/i} Then I remembered your face the first time you showed me that boiling pot sound. And I thought… if that's the memory I have to give up, forget it. I don't want to hear the future out of a cassette. I want to hear it from you, when the time comes."

translate en b36s_022:
    yara "{i}(looking at him, then breaking into a smile){/i} …That's the smartest thing that's ever come out of your mouth, Kai."

translate en b36s_023:
    kai "Every once in a while."

translate en b36s_024:
    yara "Once in a while isn't enough. Keep practicing. {i}(walking again){/i} Come on. Before the rain really hits. If we get soaked, you're carrying my bag."

translate en b36s_025:
    kai "Why does that fall on me—"

translate en b36s_026:
    yara "Because you're the one who dragged me to the shop. Come on, rek."

translate en b36s_027:
    "And that afternoon, for once, Kai walks home with his chest lighter than when he arrived — not because he knows the future, simply because he stopped trying to figure it out alone."

translate en b37_001:
    "Yara shoots up from her seat. Her breathing comes fast and sharp. All the anger that had been held back behind her tears boils right over — because now she knows everything."

translate en b37_002:
    yara "You… {i}(pointing at Kai's chest, her finger trembling){/i} You really are an idiot, Kai!"

translate en b37_003:
    kai "{i}(looking up, stunned){/i}"

translate en b37_004:
    yara "You trusted a dead spool of magnetic tape more than talking straight to me?! {i}(her voice rising sharp){/i} We spent weeks walking all over town together! Eating rawon soaking wet by the train tracks!"

translate en b37_004_p2:
    yara "Freezing up on top of that hill! I shared the sounds of the world through my own headphones, for you! And after all that, you go whispering to a cassette in a rundown shop just to peek at the future?"

translate en b37_005:
    kai "I was just scared of losing you, Yara… {i}(his voice small, hoarse){/i}"

translate en b37_006:
    yara "Scared of losing me?! {i}(cutting him off, angry tears spilling down){/i} If you're scared of losing someone, you hold on tighter to today! You don't throw away our past for a one-minute prediction that might not even happen!"

translate en b37_007:
    "Yara steps forward, forcing Kai to meet her wet eyes."

translate en b37_008:
    yara "You said that tape played me crying, saying goodbye, on August first? {i}(letting out a short, bitter laugh){/i} Of course I'm crying, Kai! Who wouldn't cry when the person they love suddenly turns cold as stone? Dodges them like they're carrying a plague? Looks right through them like a total stranger?!"

translate en b37_009:
    kai_hati "…Oh. Oh, no. Her crying… wasn't fate. She cried because of me. The tape didn't record some unavoidable future. It recorded the fallout. Because of me."

translate en b37_010:
    yara "{i}(her voice dropping low, heavy with deep disappointment){/i} You ruined our present just to brace yourself for heartbreak in the future. You traded away our very first memory — the moment I first saw you in the library — for a piece of red plastic."

translate en b37_011:
    yara "I got into my dream university, Kai. I ran over because I wanted to celebrate with you. Because I wanted us to figure out these next six months together. Instead you… you ran off and hid behind your ridiculous little prophecy."

translate en b37_012:
    "Yara wipes her tears roughly and turns toward the door."

translate en b37_013:
    yara "Magnetic tape doesn't have a soul, Kai. It can't feel the chill of the rain. It can't feel the warmth of rawon. If you'd rather live with that dead prediction — go ahead. Just don't expect me to keep standing here, waiting around for someone who can't even remember how we met."

translate en b37_014:
    "Kai is left alone in a living room that has gone dead silent. In his hand, the red cassette shell feels colder than ever — like every last drop of life inside it has evaporated."

translate en b38_001:
    "Week after week slips by without a single word between them. At school, Yara is completely out of reach now: big black headphones clamped tightly over her ears from the moment she steps off the angkot till the final bell — a wall nobody is allowed through. Especially not Kai."

translate en b38_002:
    kai_hati "Used to be me hiding behind silence. Now we traded places. Feels… fair, honestly."

translate en b38_003:
    "The calendar in Kai's bedroom flips another page. One month left until August first."

translate en b38_004:
    "Pak Ageng is finally able to get out of bed. He looks much thinner now, walking with a teak cane that creaks with every step on the floorboards. In front of Kai, a pack of onde-onde from the market has already gone cold — the sesame crust turned stiff."

translate en b38_005:
    ageng "You're supposed to eat it while it's warm. {i}(looking softly at Kai){/i} Yet you even let your food go cold. Just like you're letting all your days freeze over, Kai."

translate en b38_006:
    "Kai doesn't answer. He chews the cold onde-onde slowly, barely tasting the sweet mung bean filling inside."

translate en b38_007:
    "The next day, there's a soft clack — not someone at the door, just the mailbox on the front gate. Inside sits a white envelope with no stamp. On the front, Kai's name written in black pen. Yara's handwriting. Firm, neat."

translate en b38_008:
    kai_hati "My hands are shaking. It's just an envelope. Just an envelope."

translate en b38_009:
    yara_surat "\"Kai, I don't know if you're still listening to the sounds around you, or if you've chosen silence for good.\""

translate en b38_010:
    yara_surat "\"I'm leaving for Yogyakarta on the afternoon of August 1st, by train. My portfolio's completely finished, and the university asked me to come early for registration paperwork.\""

translate en b38_011b:
    yara_surat "\"I still remember the sentence you never finished back then, out in the rain. I've been waiting for you to finish it ever since. Maybe at the station. Maybe never.\""

translate en b38_012:
    yara_surat "\"Before I leave, I want to see you one more time. At the station, or wherever you want. I want us to talk like human beings. Not like two strangers dodging each other.\""

translate en b38_013:
    yara_surat "\"I'll wait for your reply. — Yara\""

translate en b38_014:
    kai_hati "August first. Afternoon. Train. Real. All of it's real. {i}(a long pause){/i} If I write back… if I show up at that station… I'm gonna hear her cry. I'm gonna hear that \"goodbye\" for real, with my own two ears."

translate en b38_014_p2:
    kai_hati "{i}(quieter){/i} Don't reply. If I don't show up, maybe she won't cry over me. Maybe she can leave in peace without having to look at this coward's face again."

translate en b38_015a:
    "Kai sits at his desk. A blank sheet of paper. Pen in hand."

translate en b38_016a:
    kai_hati "Draft one: \"Yara, I'm sorry.\" {i}(crossing it out){/i} Too short. Looks half-assed."

translate en b38_017a:
    "He crumples the sheet and tosses it. Draft two."

translate en b38_018a:
    kai_hati "\"Yara, all this time I—\" {i}(crossing it out again){/i} Nope. If I keep starting with myself, this letter's for me, not her."

translate en b38_019a:
    "Draft three takes the longest. He reads it over twice. Doesn't cross a single word out."

translate en b38_020a:
    kai "{i}(reading softly){/i} \"Yara. I'll come. August first, afternoon, at the station. There's a sentence I need to finish — and this time I'm finishing it.\" {i}(folding the sheet, slipping it into an envelope){/i} …Drop it off tomorrow morning. Before I change my mind."

translate en b38_015b:
    "For three days the letter sits on his desk. For three days Kai walks past it, stares at it, then finds something else to do. On the third night, late, he finally writes a short reply — far too short for everything that needed saying, yet it goes out all the same."

translate en b38_016b:
    "Her answer arrives a week later. A small envelope. One sheet. A single line right in the middle of the page, the rest blank."

translate en b38_017b:
    yara_surat "\"I didn't think you'd write back.\""

translate en b38_018b:
    kai_hati "One line. And it hits louder than everything she shouted that night."

translate en b38_015c:
    "Kai folds the letter and tucks it into his desk drawer — right beside the tangled coils of cassette tape. Fitting neighbors, he thinks. Things he can't bring himself to face, stored side by side."

translate en b38_016c:
    "He turns his phone off and puts it in the same drawer. For a whole week it stays dark. At school he keeps his head down. At home he goes to bed early. One month out from August first, Kai decides to sink completely into the silence he built himself — ignoring the last hand held out by the girl who brought his world back to life."

translate en b39_001:
    "Three weeks since that letter went into the drawer. Three weeks of Kai moving around like a ghost — watching Yara's back from down the hall, a back growing straighter, farther away."

translate en b39_001_p2:
    "This afternoon he heads back down that dry dead-end alley. Pak Ageng stands behind the counter, looking over a fresh stack of blank cassettes. He's doing much better now, though his old face still carries traces of exhaustion."

translate en b39_002:
    "Kai slumps into the wooden chair in front of the counter, burying his face in both shaking hands."

translate en b39_003:
    kai "I ruined everything, Pak. {i}(his voice breaking){/i} These past six months have been hell. I miss her. Yet I couldn't even answer her letter. I'm way too terrified of August first."

translate en b39_004:
    "Pak Ageng stops what he's doing. He sets a cassette down on the counter — clack, sharp and loud. Takes a long breath. And the look in his eyes isn't pity anymore. It's firm. Piercing."

translate en b39_005:
    ageng "You're a fool, kid."

translate en b39_006:
    kai "{i}(looking up, eyes brimming){/i} …Pak?"

translate en b39_007:
    ageng "You really are a fool. {i}(pointing at the red August 1st tape peeking out of Kai's jacket pocket){/i} You're letting a metal-coated scrap of plastic run your entire life. Treating an analog machine like some god that knows everything inside a human heart."

translate en b39_008:
    kai "But that tape recorded Yara crying, Pak! Saying goodbye to me! That's proof we're gonna end in a wreck, isn't it?!"

translate en b39_009:
    ageng "A tape records sound, Kai! Not feelings! {i}(his voice rising; dust on the glass cabinet practically trembling){/i} That machine only catches air waves. Vibrating vocal cords. Static hiss. It can't translate what's actually sitting in someone's chest when those words leave their mouth!"

translate en b39_010:
    "Pak Ageng steps closer, looking Kai dead in the eye."

translate en b39_011:
    ageng "Use the rest of your head that's still working, kid. Saying \"goodbye\" through tears can mean a dozen different things. Sure, it could be tears of parting because you threw her away like a stranger. Or it could be tears of love — someone who has to leave for a while to chase her dream, knowing the guy she loves is gonna wait faithfully till she gets back."

translate en b39_012:
    ageng "{i}(tapping the teak counter, driving home every word){/i} The exact same crying can come from hate, from heartbreak, or from love too big to fit inside normal words."

translate en b39_012_p2:
    ageng "Your red tape only told you she cried. You're the one — through every cowardly choice you're making today — deciding whether those tears are tears of regret, or tears of missing you."

translate en b39_013:
    "Kai freezes like he just got hit by a sledgehammer. All this time he'd only been listening to frequencies — never once trying to understand the soul behind the sound. He'd already waved the white flag before even understanding the melody he heard."

translate en b39_014:
    "Yara is putting together the final mix for her portfolio. On her screen and across the desk: sound files they spent months collecting. One empty slot remains right in the center of the mix — the part that will play loudest, completely on its own."

translate en b39_015:
    yara "One more. The middle's empty. Needs one sound standing completely solo right here. {i}(glancing over){/i} Which one do you think?"

translate en b39_016a:
    yara "{i}(laughing){/i} The canteen lady's boiling pot? …You know what, that's actually the most honest one. Water that can't wait to turn into steam. {i}(clicking){/i} In it goes. That's the solo."

translate en b39_016b:
    yara "Rain on the gutters… {i}(listening for a second){/i} Yeah. This is so Malang. No other city has rain that sounds quite like this. In it goes."

translate en b39_016c:
    yara "Tape hiss? {i}(pausing; then smiling faintly){/i} …Bold pick. Silence that isn't empty. Okay. I like it. In it goes."

translate en b39_017:
    "That sound gets saved dead center in the mix — and it's going to ring out clearest of all later, when the portfolio demo plays."
